From 16ea3e9622516ef727f968303ccbc03ba418a4ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:03:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Preconditioner override

The option --preconditioner-override (-pco, declared by
declareDefaultOptions) or else the environment variable
MFEM_MGIS_PRECONDITIONER_OVERRIDE, read by mfem_mgis::initialize, gives a
preconditioner which replaces the Preconditioner option of the linear
solvers set by setLinearSolver (the ones of the program, whose other
options are kept, or the linear solver override): a name (None, which
removes the option), or a map with the entries Name and Options, in the
syntax of the data of TFEL, as the linear solver override. The whole
option is replaced, wrappers included (AssembledOperator, documented). The
preconditioner of the Krylov solver of a program can thus be changed, the
program keeping its tolerances. The combinations refused by the factories
are refused with their messages; a preconditioner override can't be given
to a linear solver built by the program (a linear solver override is then
required). Both overrides are read by the same code (one function for the
factory arguments), checked across the processes of MPI and reported once;
unknown names, and None with options, are refused by
mfem_mgis::initialize.

Tests: TwoLayerCube with the preconditioner HypreDiagScale given to the
GMRES solver of the program, the preconditioner of the HyprePCG solver of
the program replaced by BoomerAMG, None given to MUMPS (2 processes), and
both overrides given by the variables (CGSolver and DSmoother,
sequential); an invalid description, an unknown name and None with
options are refused (ExecutionSettingsTest).
